{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>This thing.</b> The word <b>הַזֶּה</b> is said to mean that he heard things that are related nearby, which are the words of the wicked man who said ״הַלְהָרְגֵנִי״ etc. — not that he knew clearly that he was the one killing the Egyptian." "<b>And he sought to kill, etc.</b> Meaning, he sought to verify the matter whether he had indeed done so, in order to kill him; and therefore Moses fled from Pharaoh — lest the matter be verified and he be killed. Or it may intend, in saying <b>from Pharaoh</b>, that he recognized in his face that he was enraged, and sensed this and fled — even though he did not know that the matter had reached Pharaoh."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:32.650642704Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}